# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# WASM build outputs (wasm-bindgen-cli writes ./pkg next to the crate;
# also covers the packages/wasm/pkg/ home)
/crates/fossil-wasm/pkg/

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
.DS_Store

# Claude Code local files
CLAUDE.local.md

# The RETURNING.md ritual (CLAUDE.md) says local-only, and nothing enforced it.
RETURNING.md

# insta pending snapshots. `crates/xtask/tests/snapshot_hygiene.rs` assumes these
# never reach the history — a `.snap.new` is a proposal awaiting `cargo insta
# review`, and it is the one file that legitimately carries `assertion_line:`.
*.snap.new

# `.planning/` was ignored here. It is deleted, and the ignore goes with it: if a
# tool recreates that directory, it must show up in `git status` rather than
# accumulate a second plan out of sight. That is how the first one got to 106k lines.

# Walking-skeleton local-run artefacts.
# `fossil compile examples/hello.fossil` writes these to cwd; ignore them at
# repo root so casual smoke tests don't dirty the tree.
/output.parquet
/manifest.yaml
/.scratch-walking-skel/

# === JS/TS ecosystem (pnpm monorepo) ===
node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.next/
**/.vite/
**/.turbo/
# wasm-bindgen output is committed-elsewhere or built-on-demand, never tracked
packages/wasm/pkg/
packages/corpus/pkg/
packages/executor/pkg/
# The playground's large demo corpus: ~56 MB of Parquet written by
# `apps/playground/scripts/bench-corpus.mjs` from `apps/corpus/guards/fixture.mjs`. A build
# artifact of a private app, regenerated in about five seconds, and the generator is the
# checked-in thing rather than its output.
apps/playground/public/bench/
# Changesets are tracked on main; the `changeset version` step consumes them at
# release time. Only the empty-template fixture (if any) is ignored.
# (Earlier 08-01 ignored .changeset/*.md as "PR-bound" — corrected in 08-12 once
# the publish pipeline made tracking necessary.)
!.changeset/config.json
!.changeset/README.md
# TS incremental build state
*.tsbuildinfo

# DuckDB-WASM's spill directory. Under `NODE_RUNTIME` it defaults to `./.tmp` in
# the PROCESS's cwd, not to the OS temp dir — a `@fossil-lang/corpus` test run
# left 29 GB there on 2026-08-25 before anyone noticed. `packages/corpus`'s own
# suite now points `temp_directory` at a scratch dir it cleans up, but the
# default is the trap: any future test that boots DuckDB-WASM and touches the
# filesystem writes here, and a run that dies mid-way leaves the spill behind.
# Untracked is not enough on this repo — several sessions share one checkout and
# one git index, and an untracked directory is exactly what a careless `git add`
# sweeps up.
.tmp/

# Agent worktrees and per-user tool settings.
# `.claude/worktrees/` is git's own machinery — a checked-in worktree directory is a
# broken repository, not a stale one, so this is not the `.planning/` case above: there
# is nothing here a reviewer could ever want to read in a diff. `settings.local.json`
# is per-user by convention; a shared `settings.json` is not ignored and never should be.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
